{title: Five Loaves and Two Fish}
{subtitle: John 6:5–14; Matthew 14:15–21; Mark 6:41–44}
{key: D}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The day was long on the gras[G]sy hill, the sun was sinking [D]low
Five thousand hungry peo[G]ple and nowhere else to [D]go
Send them to the villages, the twelve said, let them [G]go and buy their bread
You give them something to [D]eat, the Master simply said
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Andrew found a little boy [G]with a basket at his side
Five barley loaves and two small [D]fish was all he could provide
But what is that among [G]so many? Andrew asked aloud
Bring them here to me, [A]said Jesus, and he looked out on the [D]crowd
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Five loaves and two [G]fish
In the Master's [D]hands
He looked up to heav[A]en, gave thanks and broke the [D]bread
And every one was [G]fed
They all ate and were [D]satisfied
[A]Twelve baskets left be[D]sides
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Have the people sit, he said, [G]there was plenty of green grass
He broke the bread and gave it out [D]to every hand to pass
From hand to hand it [G]did not end, and no one could say how
Gather up the leftover [D]pieces, so that nothing is wasted now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
What is that among so [G]many?
Bring them here to me
Little in a boy's two [D]hands
Was plenty there for all to see
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Five loaves and two [G]fish
In the Master's [D]hands
{end_of_verse}

